  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated. \nPhase changes: 903.9 K, melting point of Sb; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 4.750$ kcal/mol. \n1860 K, boiling point of Sb to equilibrium mixture of $Sb(g)$ , $Sb_{2}(g)$ , and $Sb_{4}(g)$ . \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-3000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 25.718 + 0.054 \\times 10^{-3} T - 2.021 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=25.718\\times10^{-3}T+0.027\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+2.021\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-8.348$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-903.9 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = 5.933 + 2.111 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 3.809 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 198.600 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = 5.933 - 2.111 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 3.809 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 99.300 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 3.029 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n903.9-1860 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -4.577 - 5.125 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.293 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 133.800 T^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = -4.577 + 5.125 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.293 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 66.900 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 31.378 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data based on Prusaczyk (101) who estimated molecular constants. ",
